 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 2,
  "text": "Lint and standards now pass. I haven't run a build, so I don't know whether synthesis accepts the new `.vlt` file in the sources.\n\n- **Lint:** the two warnings were in the supplied `data/jtag_bus.sv`, which I can't edit. Verilator applies in-file `lint_off` pragmas per file, so the pragmas in `rtl/top.sv` and `rtl/xilinx_sim_stubs.sv` never reached it. I added `rtl/jtag_bus_waiver.vlt`, a Verilator config waiver for UNUSEDSIGNAL on that one file, and listed it in `build.yaml`. It is wrapped in `ifdef VERILATOR`, so Icarus ignores it. I also edited the comments in `rtl/xilinx_sim_stubs.sv` and dropped its `lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL` line. That edit didn't fix anything on its own and could be reverted.\n- **Standards:** the STD-CDC-01 \"inline_in jtag_bus\" error no longer shows. `architecture.yaml` already says `inline_in: top`, so I changed nothing there, and `gates(kind=\"standards\")` shows STD-CDC-01 as ok. That run still ends in FAIL: the three post-synthesis rules (STD-CLK-03, STD-CDC-02, STD-METH-01) were not run because there are no synthesis reports yet, and three review rules are listed as review only.\n- **Not run:** the `cdc` check needs a synthesised design. I did not run the full `check` with `names: [\"all\"]`, or simulation.\n\nDONE."
 },
